1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,620
He rose from an artillery officer

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:05,640
to become the most feared
ruler in Europe.

3
00:00:05,890 --> 00:00:07,720
Napoleon Bonaparte crowned himself

4
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:10,470
Emperor of the French
in 1804.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:12,640
His armies won
extraordinary victories,

6
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,940
and his empire
reshaped the continent.

7
00:00:15,190 --> 00:00:17,230
But Napoleon wanted more.

8
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:19,590
In 1812, he invaded Russia

9
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:21,700
with a vast
multinational army.

10
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:23,100
He reached Moscow,

11
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:26,170
only to find much of the city
burning.

12
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:28,470
Then came the retreat.

13
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:29,880
Hunger, disease, exhaustion,

14
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:32,220
and bitter cold
devastated his forces.

15
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:34,150
His enemies united.

16
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,120
In 1814, Napoleon abdicated

17
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,260
and was exiled to Elba.

18
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:40,460
He returned the following year

19
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:42,010
for one final gamble.

20
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:45,030
At Waterloo,
his army was defeated.

21
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:49,090
This time, exile meant
a remote island in the Atlantic:

22
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:49,850
Saint Helena.

23
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:52,530
Napoleon died there
in 1821.

24
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:54,720
He conquered kingdoms,
changed Europe,

25
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:56,280
and became a legend.

26
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:58,450
But he could not conquer

27
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:00,750
the consequences
of his own ambition.

